      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{64524e889511692a74619c99|full_name} New instances work but still come with the added friction typically associated. Large events that are hard to get into may lose people who already waited in queue for the first instance. Or if theres a sudden spike in attendance when you're already in the middle of a performance, you would have to move everyone, including the performer while they're busy etc. \n\nGranted, I also know that if it was a simple flick of a switch to add this they likely would have included it and given the wider needs of the platform it's totally understandable to not make this a priority nor am I personally expecting them to. I figured at the very least though, a canny helps gauge how interested people actually are in this and by extension how much it is/isnt worth devoting time and resources to when compared against the amount of effort it would theoretically take.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
